hat tracks the order of attributes, because this is used below in `mergeOutputAttributes`. Using the `AttributeMap` could lead to funky errors in case of attribute shadowing in the groupings.","The role of AttributeMap is to guarantee equality - while it can deal with ordering (it\u0027s a linkedmap), it\u0027s better to have this recorded elsewhere such as a list.","Ah, fair point; however, there shouldn\u0027t be groupings with same name id but different names, so the `mergeOutputAttributes` below should take care of deduplicating fine.\r\n\r\nI think using the `AttributeMap` here is less obvious (I completely forgot the thing preserves iteration order), esp. since an `AttributeSet` seems to suffice."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java","id":37259,"created_at":"2024-08-06T12:50:02Z","original_position":21,"side":"LEFT","position":29,"submitted_on_commit":"a18846c3a374cc8f6c18bf9cab43a4d807de4d66","diff_hunk":"@@ -458,17 +456,17 @@ private LogicalPlan resolveStats(Stats stats, List\u003cAttribute\u003e childrenOutput) {\n                 }\n             }\n \n-            if (stats.expressionsResolved() \u003d\u003d false) {\n-                AttributeMap\u003cExpression\u003e resolved \u003d new AttributeMap\u003c\u003e();","submitted_line":462},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"I have reviewed all the changes in this chapter. The modifications primarily focus on improving the handling of union types (ambiguous field mappings) by allowing them to propagate through certain analysis phases and providing more descriptive \"Unsupported\" errors instead of generic \"Unresolved\" errors when they cannot be resolved.\nThe refactoring in `Analyzer.ResolveRefs#resolveStats` (#0X6BJ) correctly simplifies the collection of resolved attributes, and the updates to `TypeResolutions` (#ETZGN, #FS04S) properly implement the logic for validating union types against predicates. The removal of redundant re-resolution log